.nh
.TH "ANVILD" "8" "Sep 2026" "Anvil" "Anvil Manual"

.SH NAME
anvild \- daemon that drives QEMU VMs and Docker/Podman containers for anvil

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanvild\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION
anvild is the daemon behind \fBanvil\fR(1) and \fBanvil tui\fR. It owns every
instance's lifecycle, the image vault, and the on-disk registry, and exposes
all of it over gRPC on a unix socket; the CLI and TUI are dumb clients that
just build a request and send it over that socket.

It drives QEMU processes directly over QMP for VMs (no libvirt) and talks to
Docker's real HTTP API for containers (no SDK). It takes no command-line
flags or subcommands; its on-disk layout is fixed and its runtime behavior is
controlled entirely through the requests it receives over the socket.

On startup it creates its run, state, and cache directories if missing,
opens its registry, reconciles instance and intent-network state against
what's actually running, and starts listening. For every intent with a
shared network it also serves DNS on port 53 of that network's gateway
address, answering \fI<role>\fR.\fI<intent>\fR.anvil for each member and
forwarding other names to the resolvers in \fB/etc/resolv.conf\fR. Binding
port 53 needs \fBCAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE\fR. It shuts down gracefully on
\fBSIGINT\fR or \fBSIGTERM\fR, waiting up to 10 seconds for in-flight RPCs
(such as \fBanvil logs --follow\fR) to finish before forcing a stop.

.SH FILES
.PP
\fB/run/anvil/anvild.sock\fP
.RS 4
The gRPC unix socket the CLI and TUI connect to. Created mode 0660, group
\fBanvil\fR, so any member of that group can reach the daemon without root.
.RE
.PP
\fB/var/lib/anvil/anvil.db\fP
.RS 4
bbolt registry: instances, intents, images, mirrors, hosts, and the saved
cloud-init library.
.RE
.PP
\fB/var/lib/anvil/instances/\fP
.RS 4
Per-instance mutable state that doesn't belong in the registry (VM disks,
container volumes).
.RE
.PP
\fB/var/lib/anvil/.ssh/id_ed25519\fP
.RS 4
Passwordless ed25519 keypair anvild uses as the SSH client identity for
\fBanvil migrate\fR. Generated once on install; the matching public key has
to be added to \fB~/.ssh/authorized_keys\fR on any host used as a migration
target.
.RE
.PP
\fB/var/cache/anvil/images/prepared/\fP
.RS 4
Downloaded and checksum-verified base VM images.
.RE
.PP
\fB/etc/anvil/\fP
.RS 4
Reserved for daemon configuration; unused today.
.RE

.SH RUNNING
anvild is meant to run under systemd as the unprivileged \fBanvil\fR system
user, not root; the packaged \fBanvild.service\fR unit grants it just enough
capabilities for KVM and tap/bridge networking. It isn't started
automatically on install:
.PP
.RS 4
\fBsystemctl enable --now anvild\fP
.RE
.PP
Access control is unix group membership plus socket reachability: adding a
user to the \fBanvil\fR group is what grants it the ability to talk to
anvild, there are no accounts, no portal, and no password.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanvil\fR(1), \fBanvil-migrate\fR(1), \fBsystemctl\fR(1)
